----------------- Database Partioning & Sharding -----------------------

Partioning : It is a process of splitting a large database or table into smaller partitions.

Why this is needed ??
When we see industrial data , millions of data is present and millions of data is getting created and then we have to query on a million/billion rows, this becomes very difficult.

1.SO properly scaling the data and improving the query performance/query optimization
2.Large database efficiency


eg. we have a cake and in order everyone get a slice we cut the cake and give to all

same happens with the DB.

Types of Partioning:
1.Horizontal Partioning - division based on rows/records
2.Vertical - column based (schema management becomes easy)
3.Functional - (eg on ecommerce site - order table, user table is seperate )
4.Key Based - one column amm custid so based on this column value like 1-10k in one table and so on
5.Range Based - db has some timestamp so based on some amm timeline or timerange lets say we divide he data
6.Hash Based - we do hashing here by creating a hashing
7.Round Robin Partioning - here we didivde data cyclically and equally distributed among partitions (it balances the data well)



