**************************************** DATABASE REPLICATION ********************************

always try to understand WHY?
in intv also always ask why this , why that?

Why database replication is required?

because a db can go down or some data can get lost or , hack may be

so we should be having copies to recover it, eg if banks loose their ata then how to tell which person has how much amount of money,  if an ecmmerce site loose their data and you want to return something how they will know yourpast history.

so its imp to keep copies of data and storing them in multiple places

ok so why its needed ? 
-High avalability
-Fault Tolerance
-Read Scalability
-Disaster Recovery


Types of Replication:
1.Synchronous Replication
2.Async
3.Semi-Synch

Sync :  DB1 (Master)
       |    | replicas
       DB2  DB3

so all data comes to master db is send to replicas
so in sync immediate write happens to replicas

and due to this
-Data consistency happens

so whereever data consistency is very imp so we go with this like in banks

cons: Slower writes , overall write operations is slower and lots of writes happening to different replicas

ASYNC Partition :

-writes to replica happens in background
-we move to next write after master confirmation only


so it provides :
-faster writes

cons : Temporary loose consistency



Semi-Synch Partition:

-here at least one replica to acknowledge about write


---------- Replication Models -------------

-Single Leader
-Multi Leader
-Leader less



1.Single Leader (Master | Slave or  Primary | Secondary)

write happens on single leader or master
and read from slaves/secondary db's

2.Multi-leader

here multiple nodes are handling the write


write happens on multiple leaders and then they copy the data to next leaders
-it provides high read avalability
-write conflict resoloution is tough


3.Leader less:

you can write to any replica
-it is always available

Dynamodb and cassandra allows this




..............Read-Write Strategies...........
1.Write should happen only on leaders
2.read should happen on replicas

3.Replication lag : the time it take to write on the db, so if that time is more than replication lag is more so we have to actively monitor the replication lag




 .................... All DB's we have...............

 1.Mysql : Master-Slave or Primary-Secondary and we have to manually create this
 2.MongoDB : Replica - Set   leader election is automated
 3.Cassandra : Leaderless  but we can tune the consistency here
 4.Dynamo : leaderless v and it is eventually consistent









